---
// Architecture of AI-Gateway-API as implemented in the repository (app/ folder).
// `compact` shows the question-answering path and providers only.
import Flow from "./Flow.astro";

type Props = { compact?: boolean };
const { compact = false } = Astro.props;

const errors = [
	{ code: "504", label: "Timeout" },
	{ code: "503", label: "Unavailable" },
	{ code: "429", label: "Rate limited + Retry-After" },
	{ code: "502", label: "Anything else" },
];
---

<figure class="space-y-4" aria-label="AI Gateway API architecture">
	{
		!compact && (
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow mb-2">POST /documents</p>
				<Flow
					steps={[
						{ label: "Chunk text", detail: "overlapping windows" },
						{ label: "Embed chunks", detail: "Gemini embeddings" },
						{ label: "Store", detail: "vector store" },
					]}
				/>
			</div>
		)
	}

	<div>
		<p class="eyebrow mb-2">POST /ask</p>
		<Flow
			steps={[
				{ label: "Embed question", detail: "query embedding" },
				{ label: "Rank chunks", detail: "cosine, top-k" },
				{ label: "Score ≥ threshold?", detail: "grounding check" },
				{ label: "Answer + sources", detail: "cites [1], [2]" },
			]}
		/>
		<p class="mt-2 rounded-xl border border-dashed border-line px-3 py-2 font-mono text-[11px] leading-snug text-muted">
			nothing relevant → "not found", model never called
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
		<div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface px-3 py-2.5">
			<p class="text-[13px] font-medium">GeminiProvider</p>
			<p class="mt-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
				chat + embeddings<br />timeout per request<br />retry 429 / 500 / 503, backoff + jitter
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-line px-3 py-2.5">
			<p class="text-[13px] font-medium">MockProvider</p>
			<p class="mt-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
				offline, deterministic<br />no API key needed<br />powers the 44 tests
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	{
		!compact && (
			<>
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow mb-2">Typed errors → HTTP</p>
					<ul class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 sm:grid-cols-4">
						{errors.map(({ code, label }) => (
							<li class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface px-3 py-2">
								<p class="font-mono text-sm font-medium text-accent">{code}</p>
								<p class="text-[11px] leading-snug text-muted">{label}</p>
							</li>
						))}
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow mb-2">/ask response</p>
					<pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface px-3 py-2.5 font-mono text-[12px] leading-relaxed"><code>{`{ "answer": "… [1]", "grounded": true,
  "sources": [{ "doc_id": "…", "chunk_id": "…", "score": …, "preview": "…" }],
  "model": "…", "usage": { "input_tokens": …, "output_tokens": … },
  "latency": … }`}</code></pre>
				</div>
			</>
		)
	}
	<figcaption class="sr-only">
		Documents sent to POST /documents are chunked, embedded and stored. POST /ask embeds the question, ranks stored chunks by
		cosine similarity and keeps those above a threshold. If none remain, it answers "not found" without calling the model;
		otherwise the model answers from the numbered chunks and cites them. Providers retry 429, 500 and 503 responses with
		exponential backoff and jitter, and errors map to 504, 503, 429 or 502.
	</figcaption>
</figure>
